PARITY MAPPING (web lib/globalShortcuts.tsx  ->  native)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The web `GlobalShortcuts` is a HEADLESS REGISTRAR: it reads useTranslation, builds
the canonical shortcut definitions, pours them into the registry via useShortcut(defs)
so the cheatsheet has a single source of truth, and renders null. The native surface
reproduces BOTH roles: it registers the identical definitions (registrar) AND renders
the discoverable grouped cheatsheet the registry feeds (reader) — never a blank box.

  Data sources (bound via P1/S8 state holders):
    useTranslation  -> GlobalShortcutsStrings facade (P1/S10)
    useShortcut     -> GlobalShortcutsSource.register(defs) + registry snapshot

  Canonical definitions (21 = 4 + 14 + 3), verbatim from the web sources:
    Actions (4)     Ctrl+K / "/" / "?" / "Esc"          (web `universals`)
    Navigation (14) every GOTO_SHORTCUTS entry as g+<key> (useKeyboardShortcuts.ts)
    Commands (3)    every commandRegistry entry with a `shortcut` hint
                    (T -> themePicker, ? -> shortcuts, E -> dashboardEdit)

  i18n keys from source (all present in globalShortcuts.strings):
    shortcuts.groups.actions / .navigation / .commands
    shortcuts.openPalette / .openPaletteAlt / .openShortcuts / .close / .goto

  States (every one renders — no hidden surface):
    loading / empty / error / data + orthogonal connection axis (live/stale/offline)
    with a one-shot auto-refresh on the stale transition.

